  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The KSX search fund segment has become the primary growth engine, outpacing legacy extended warranty operations. Acquisitions are driving strong momentum, and Q1 results exceeded internal expectations, reflecting solid demand for niche, recurring-revenue services. The stock’s recent decline, however, indicates market caution, creating a mixed picture where improving business trends have yet to lift shares.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management continues to execute its distinctive public search fund strategy, using permanent capital and a tax-advantaged structure to compound asset-light service businesses. The KSX segment has reached critical scale, with the acquisition flywheel self-reinforcing. Quarterly beats and confident commentary enhance credibility, but the market remains in “prove it” mode; sustained delivery could eventually close the value gap.",
